# Repo-root ignore rules. The repo is two layers (same shape as
# personal-assistant / DASHBOARD-164):
#   walls/    — host-only config the agent must never touch (NOT mounted into
#               the container): the sandbox definition, egress allowlist, secrets.
#   sandbox/  — the agent's world, mounted into the container at /work.
# Codebase ignore rules live in sandbox/.gitignore. This file covers the walls
# layer + machine-global noise.

# Walls — host-only sandbox config that's never committed:
#   walls/.env          host-only toggles (sourced by up.sh); template is tracked
#   walls/secrets/*      real Claude OAuth creds / GitHub deploy keys (volumes)
walls/.env
walls/secrets/*
!walls/secrets/.gitignore
!walls/secrets/README.md

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Editors
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# sandbox/ is its own repo — the agent codebase mounted at /work. This outer
# repo is the host-only walls layer; it does not track the sandbox.
/sandbox/
